      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think a test for a filegroup with aidl and non-aidl srcs make sense because the scenario results to BUILD output that\u0027s invalid (e.g. filegroup macro with both AIDL and non-AIDL sources).\n\n[Here](https://android-review.googlesource.com/c/platform/build/soong/+/2186599/5/android/filegroup.go#76), I intentionally skip converting such scenario to aidl_library and suggest that we manually split the filegroup in Android.bp instead. I think a filegroup with a mixed bag of AIDL and non-AIDL isn\u0027t a good practice to do in Android.bp because the path prop becomes multi-purposed (it can either proto path, or aidl package path).\n\nLet me know if you have more comment.",
